WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Start with an LLM agent. It proposes a concept and how actions change it. The completed scene moves into the first panel of the process figure.

00:08.000 --> 00:16.000
Learn from what changes. Demonstrated transitions supervise the visual classifier, without hand-labeled concept annotations. This scene joins the agent in the figure.

00:16.000 --> 00:26.000
Feedback makes it a loop. The agent reads learning and validation feedback and revises its next proposal. The feature animation is schematic.

00:26.000 --> 00:34.000
The result is a concept the robot can recognize: a visual predicate that provides facts for a planner. The concept scene completes the four-part figure.

00:34.000 --> 00:40.000
The full process: agent proposals, learning from demonstrations, feedback-driven refinement, and learned visual concepts.

00:40.000 --> 01:26.375
Complete table-cleaning demonstration: pick and place three toys into the box, grasp the towel, then wipe away the debris. Original footage at three times recorded speed.
